From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Taron <philip.taron@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:15:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Report readers waiting on the card over Varlink

A card that needs more time answers a command with CCID time extensions
until it is done. Security keys do this while they wait for a touch: a
YubiKey 5 sends one about 200 ms after a PIV GENERAL AUTHENTICATE that
needs a touch, then one every 290 ms or so until it is touched.

Nothing outside pcscd can see that, because pcscd holds the USB device.
So report it: with libsystemd 257 or later, libccid now serves the
Varlink interface io.github.philiptaron.CcidTouch on /run/pcscd/ccid-touch
(see the varlink-address option). Its Watch method, called with the
"more" flag, reports every reader waiting now and then streams

  {"device": "usb:1050/0406:libudev:1:/dev/bus/usb/001/002", "waiting": true}

when a reader starts receiving time extensions, and "waiting": false when
the card answers, the exchange fails, or the reader is closed.

The reader threads only update a table and poke an eventfd; a thread of
our own runs the Varlink server and sends the changes, since sd-varlink
is not thread safe. The socket is world-accessible: it only says that
some reader is waiting.

The feature is optional (varlink=auto) and not built into libccidtwin.
